# Line endings.
#
# Prettier expects LF (its `endOfLine` default), and the repo stores LF. A
# Windows checkout with git's `core.autocrlf=true` — the default on GitHub's
# Windows runners — rewrites every file to CRLF, and `eslint .` then reports a
# `Delete ␍` warning on every line of every file. `eol=lf` pins the working
# tree to LF on every platform, so CI and a local Windows clone agree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize, never diff as text. The image and font
# list is the house list (balor, HTOO-236); the last three are Epona's own.
*.png binary
*.bmp binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.pdf binary
*.node binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
